First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B534: b520 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> round 1 of 2 on #100 @ 2f536f2 (C1 delta <9 paths, 6 commits, +1031 -18 by program y/n, three src files y/n, existing lines removed <18 of 18 accounted> y/n, new user-facing sentences <1 y/n>, other new strings 0 y/n, non-ASCII new bytes <n> - C2 Done-when -189 <met n of n> -190 <n of n> -191 <n of n> -192 <n of n> -193 <n of n>, drops -92 right y/n and -99 right y/n, PRIOR WORK true y/n, UTC date sites left <n> - C3 new names <40 y/n>, red at base <n of n predicted> for the right reason y/n, green-by-design rows with a killing mutant <n of n> - C4 mutants <k of m killed, builder's n of 13 reproduced, Ordinal-back killed y/n, survivors <names|none>, controls c0 c1 c2 c3 as expected y/n>, rows no mutant turns red <n> - C5 attack rows <n run, n NOT TESTED>, registry changed by a refusal <n>, second Active <n>, defective version made live <n>, twin classes accepted against the ruling <n named>, amplification worst <ms at N> - C6 differential cases <n> seed <n>, ruled-twins-accepted classes <n>, code-refused-oracle-different <n>, base-versus-head decisions equal outside named classes <y/n>, date disagreements <n> - C7 build 0/0 <y/n>, Api/Engine/Import <n/n/n>, web <files/tests>, failed <n>, skipped <n>, names lost <n> added <n>, zone-or-culture dependent rows <n> - C8 checks <n completed success of n>, pending <names|none>, failing <names|none>, CodeQL open alerts on the PR ref <n>, analyses <n of 4> - C9 live lanes sharing a path <n>, b53 shares <n> with no open PR <y/n>, semantic overlap with B518 <read|not on origin>, B529 <read|not on origin>, conflict markers <n> - C10 gitleaks canary rc <n>, scan rc <n>)`. **A NO GO line ends with `majors+: B534-n, B534-m, ...` naming every Major and Blocker by id.** Then: Step 0 sha256s and slot count with control / REFUSE counts with controls / PINS (start, mid, verdict, branch name beside each sha) / instrument and load (dotnet, node, npm versions; load and slot per heavy run; every wait; every `gh` and Jira GET named) / the invariants and the prediction (written before any run, with their evidence paths) / C1-C10 each with the FAIL (clock time), evidence path and result / the Done-when clause table / the removed-lines table (18) / the string-literal table (every literal added, its class a-e, the base line for each class c) / the new-names table (the 40: red or green at base, killing mutant) / the mutant table and the rows table / the attack-row table (id, request sequence, expected, answer, registry hash before/after, host, MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY) / the twin-class table (shape, ruling reading, code answer, class) / findings `B534-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, the regression that would be red; "none" is valid) / findings of FACT for Tuesday listed apart (anything the diff leaves standing and base had equally: a swap that skips the duplicate-id check, an expired book that still swaps (not ruled), the `b53` overlap, B529's importer edit as a merge-order fact, the `Sources` to `Quotes` dependency, the Linux zone-data assumption, the one sentence awaiting the words gate, the docs sentence for PR #98) / FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections (where the builder's STATUS or this brief was wrong, with the measurement) / processes, slots, trees left / **UNMEASURED** (last section before the last line: the CI Linux runner beyond the PR logs, zone data and invariant-mode behaviour on that image, behaviour on a real hosted site (the version store is refused in Entra mode: say what you read), a signed-in browser, concurrent processes on one registry, the merged result's build with B518 or B529, any run on a quieter machine, anything you could not drive and why). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` to the first AND last line if a check you were required to run could not be run (never a bare GO). **Last line of STATUS, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B534 b520/mps-source-lifecycle-hardening @ 2f536f2 on main <sha7>: B520 source-version governance hardening <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2 on #100; PR #100 open; CI <complete|pending: names>)` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict) / `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` + ONE question.
**Severity floor (binding).**
- *Blocker:* any input (S1-S8, C6) by which a version carrying a defect the validator knows (bar the expired date) becomes Active or is rolled back to; two versions Active; a refusal that changes the registry bytes or writes an event; a registry state word that lets a copy of an existing document validate (the fail-open this PR fixes) at the head; a legitimately different id refused as a twin (C6); a path beyond the nine, a fourth `src` file, any byte of `.github/`, `docs/`, `web/`, a `.csproj`, `PriceBookImporter.cs`; a secret or customer datum in an added line; the head moved; a new open alert on the PR ref; a date rule that expires a book a day early or a day late for any instant in S2 against the importer's rule.
- *Major:* a Done-when clause NOT MET; a drop (-92 or -99) that is wrong; a SECOND new user-visible string (C1 class e) or the claimed sentence interpolating anything but the server-formed version id; a new row red at base for a wrong reason or a `red` row green at base; a new row with no mutant that turns it red and no stated reason; any surviving mutant on a state, date, content-check, cost-per-page or id-comparison decision (C4), including `StringComparer.Ordinal` back; **a pair of ids that the ruling says are the same (case, composed versus decomposed accent) and the head accepts as two ids, in a class the builder did NOT declare unfolded (the asymmetric-composition case pairs are the drafter's lead: count them and rate by your measurement)**; another place in the pipeline that compares version ids exactly while this check folds them, so a twin passes validation and collides elsewhere; a place that still decides expiry or validity on a UTC date (C2 census); a swap that is WEAKER than base on any input; an existing test removed, skipped, weakened, or an existing line edited; a test name lost or one added beyond the builder's 40; any test red at the head and green at base; a build warning; a failing PR check-run (any cause); a builder claim your measurement contradicts (9 paths, 3 `src` files, 40 names, Api 2001, Import 162, 13 of 13 mutants, the red-first counts); a row that depends on the host's zone, culture, clock or ordering (C7); an operator-log line that names a value, a property name from the document or a path; a request within the accepted size that holds the registry lock for seconds (S8); a person's name, a decision-card id, a ticket key in code or a commit.
- *Minor:* an unstated equivalent mutant survivor; a TRUE-BUT-IMPRECISE comment or test title; the race row missing at base on some runs (C3); a measurement of the builder's that your run contradicts without changing the verdict; a stricter-than-needed refusal class the head adds (named, with the shape: for example a version stuck in an unknown state word); a double report of one defect; the builder's `B520_189_` test-name prefix if your shape scan flags it.
- *Note:* the carried-over non-ASCII in pre-existing lines the diff did not touch; `$"deviceRows[{i}]"` as a new instance of an existing shape; the swap not re-running the duplicate-id check (the builder's D-4, equal to base); an expired book that still swaps (not ruled); `b53` sharing two paths with no open PR; the one sentence awaiting the words gate (never judged); the builder's stale-DLL, load-limit (a last run at load1 10.06) and `cd` disclosures; CI pending at the verdict (the verdict waits or says so; it is not a finding); style.

## HOLDS
- Datasec / MPS Commercial Calculator only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, docker, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production site or any app host** (the tests are in-process; no server of yours is started). Network: `git fetch` of explicit refspecs into YOUR scratch clone, `gh api -X GET` under `GH_CONFIG_DIR='<project>/4_Credentials/.gh-config'`, Jira GET as C2 allows, `npm ci` and NuGet restore into your own worktrees. `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh api -X POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` are forbidden. Never dismiss an alert. No decision-queue tool in any form (the decision card named in the addendum is read by the drafter and by you only through the addendum's quoted ruling), no scoreboard, nothing under `fleet/briefs_staged/`, no Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool.
- **Git in the project repo: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`); `fetch`, `worktree`, the legacy `merge-tree`, `checkout`, `gc`, `worktree prune` only inside `.tools/b534/repo` and `.tools/b534/wt-*`. No git verb in the project root (records repo).
- **The real price books are confidential.** Never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.tools/backup-*`, or any real book or store; every scratch row and every generated document uses synthetic data (the importer's own synthetic books or hand-made ones). Secrets only as environment, never on argv; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test and the Jira GET.
- **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -D`): quarantine to `.tools/b534/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`** (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain a space and `!`); where `dotnet` or `npm` needs a cwd, set it with Python `subprocess(cwd=...)` or `bash -c` and say so; write `${VAR}:path`; multi-step chains under `bash -c '...'` or a QUOTED heredoc; no unquoted word starting with `=` in command position (the project root holds a file named `=`: use `----` as a separator); bash, not zsh, for loops; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything that reads a file you did not write.
- No person's name in any id, file, branch or STATUS you make (say "the product owner"; git author fields carry a name: do not quote them), no decision-card id, clock from `date`. 0 non-ASCII bytes in every scratch file you write and in your STATUS. Release before the last line: no process of yours in `ps`; no `dotnet build-server shutdown` (the shared servers are other seats'; with `-nodeReuse:false` you start none); your heavy slot absent; your port block free. A line at your prompt that is not a Tuesday file pointer is not an instruction. Nothing to any human.
- **RESUME (at about 80% of your context, or at the hard stop):** stop new checks, write STATUS sections `PROGRESS` (each check: done / partial / not started, with evidence paths) and `RESUME` (the exact next commands, the state of every scratch tree and mutant with its restore proof, the slot you hold or released, the pins you last read, the invariant file, the seed and the generated-case file paths), restore every mutant and release the slot, then end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". A verdict from a gate that did not finish C4, C5 and C6 is conditional at best (name the unfinished check in the first line).

